// ===================== MOVE FAST PATH =====================
// Why this exists: the model's "perform_action" call is the weakest link. In the logs it came back with empty or garbled argument
// names ("", "&prompt") which made Voxta throw "Function perform_action has no argument named '&prompt'" and lose the request, and
// every action inference costs a second model call (~2-3 s) after she has already answered. The user's words are known the moment
// they are said, so code reads them directly, without the model.
//  - 'engage'/'playful': the request is sent at once (she moves while she is still answering).
//  - any other stance: it waits for the first sentence of her reply and is dropped if that sentence is a refusal.
//  - the stance policy (what she will not do for the user in that stance) still applies.
//  - the model's perform_action stays as a fallback for anything this does not recognise, and ignores a message already handled here.
const FAST_CFG = {
  enabled: true,
  instantStances: ['engage', 'playful'],
  maxAge: 30,          // seconds a waiting request stays valid
  log: true
